      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/coyrdoras-paleatus-wild-2/",
      "html": "<p>Corydoras paleatus is widespread in southern South America. Wild-caught fish are only very rarely imported. Imports of this species did not appear for more than 10 years, because many export stations in southern Brazil had to close down when some of the most important ornamental fishes of the region were left off the Brazilian positive list, which regulated which species could be caught and exported as ornamental fish. Now a negative list is in effect, meaning that all species may again be caught and exported unless they are specially protected.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/coyrdoras-paleatus-wild-2/",
      "html": "<p>This veteran among aquarium fishes was already bred in 1878 by the Parisian aquarium pioneer Pierre Carbonnier. Outside France the species has been available since 1893. Since then there have always been offspring, and various breeding forms (long-finned, albino etc.) are always available in the trade.</p>"
    }
  ],
